1
00:00:07,626 --> 00:00:09,896
(Space Rice Cake)

2
00:00:10,150 --> 00:00:11,880
(Leaving their beloved Goheung behind, )

3
00:00:12,120 --> 00:00:14,020
(they arrived in Seoul.)

4
00:00:14,390 --> 00:00:19,590
(With their fierce ambition, they conquered Seoul...)

5
00:00:19,820 --> 00:00:22,660
(and made a glamorous opening for Space Rice Cake's 2nd branch.)

6
00:00:22,960 --> 00:00:25,300
(Along with its grand exterior, it features a larger kitchen...)

7
00:00:25,530 --> 00:00:28,330
(filled with upgraded equipment.)

8
00:00:28,600 --> 00:00:30,870
(On the 2nd floor, you'll find an expanded dining area.)

9
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:33,000
(Overwhelmed by the massive scale, the members were having a meltdown.)

10
00:00:33,100 --> 00:00:35,109
(To help the members manage the shop, )

11
00:00:35,110 --> 00:00:36,740
(Manager Kwon's special training began.)

12
00:00:37,040 --> 00:00:38,979
(Beef burger)

13
00:00:38,980 --> 00:00:40,880
(Shrimp burger)

14
00:00:41,110 --> 00:00:42,810
(Mint carrot cake)

15
00:00:42,950 --> 00:00:45,580
(The eye-popping flavor...)

16
00:00:45,850 --> 00:00:48,420
(that makes you hum)

17
00:00:48,520 --> 00:00:50,620
(The Seoul branch menu has been completely mastered!)

18
00:00:50,820 --> 00:00:52,960
(8 hours have passed since they clocked in amidst the chaos.)

19
00:00:53,930 --> 00:00:55,289
I can't make up my mind.

20
00:00:55,290 --> 00:00:56,659
- Can we prep something now?
- I think we can make...

21
00:00:56,660 --> 00:00:58,029
- wasabi mayonnaise.
- We can do that tomorrow.

22
00:00:58,030 --> 00:00:59,429
Can we just make the sauce before going home?

23
00:00:59,430 --> 00:01:01,700
(Therefore, today...)

24
00:01:02,030 --> 00:01:03,499
We should make basil mayonnaise...

25
00:01:03,500 --> 00:01:05,739
- and wasabi mayonnaise.
- What were you trying to say?

26
00:01:05,740 --> 00:01:06,809
- It won't take long.
- Which one takes a long time?

27
00:01:06,810 --> 00:01:08,109
- It won't take long.
- It won't.

28
00:01:08,110 --> 00:01:09,909
- Wait. Hold on a second.
- Yes?

29
00:01:09,910 --> 00:01:11,140
We have to...

30
00:01:11,340 --> 00:01:12,640
We forgot about tteoksagna.

31
00:01:13,010 --> 00:01:14,410
(Laughing in disbelief)

32
00:01:14,510 --> 00:01:15,610
Oh, tteoksagna?

33
00:01:16,250 --> 00:01:17,580
Since I have to make tteokbokki tomorrow,

34
00:01:17,980 --> 00:01:20,220
I have to prep for it. I have to make broth.

35
00:01:20,590 --> 00:01:23,459
(Additional prep 2: Tteokbokki)

36
00:01:23,460 --> 00:01:25,320
(They're working late tonight!)

37
00:01:25,920 --> 00:01:27,859
- Working all day long - Oh, yes.

38
00:01:27,860 --> 00:01:29,129
All day long

39
00:01:29,130 --> 00:01:30,559
- I'm going to go get it - Saving my knees

40
00:01:30,560 --> 00:01:31,760
Red, red

41
00:01:32,000 --> 00:01:33,130
Gosh, I'm tired.

42
00:01:34,100 --> 00:01:35,199
What?

43
00:01:35,200 --> 00:01:36,940
(They just started working, and she's already grumbling.)

44
00:01:37,300 --> 00:01:38,399
Saving my knees

45
00:01:38,400 --> 00:01:39,570
- Red, red - Red, red

46
00:01:40,570 --> 00:01:41,609
- Celery, celery - My knees

47
00:01:41,610 --> 00:01:42,710
Green, green

48
00:01:43,340 --> 00:01:45,309
POS system, POS system, green, green

49
00:01:45,310 --> 00:01:46,379
Hand-writing, hand-writing

50
00:01:46,380 --> 00:01:47,479
- Red, red - Red

51
00:01:47,480 --> 00:01:48,549
Standing up, standing up

52
00:01:48,550 --> 00:01:49,579
- Red, red - Yes, yes

53
00:01:49,580 --> 00:01:50,619
Sitting down, sitting down

54
00:01:50,620 --> 00:01:51,779
- Green, green - Green, green

55
00:01:51,780 --> 00:01:52,850
(The labor songs these days express resentment.)

56
00:01:53,490 --> 00:01:55,020
Hang in there, Prince.

57
00:01:55,890 --> 00:01:57,159
Thank you, Queen.

58
00:01:57,160 --> 00:01:59,619
- Should I call her "Mom?"
- "Mom?"

59
00:01:59,620 --> 00:02:02,089
- It should be "Mother."
- Right, "Mother."

60
00:02:02,090 --> 00:02:03,860
(The Tteokbokki Prince is oblivious to the rules of the palace.)

61
00:02:04,330 --> 00:02:07,030
Chef, can't we just have some fun while doing the prep work?

62
00:02:07,500 --> 00:02:09,870
- Shall we make it fun?
- Yes.

63
00:02:10,100 --> 00:02:11,899
- Who's your bias? I'm your bias - I'm your bias

64
00:02:11,900 --> 00:02:14,239
- Who's your bias? I'm your bias - Who's your bias?

65
00:02:14,240 --> 00:02:17,180
- I'm your bias - Let's lower the key.

66
00:02:17,610 --> 00:02:19,110
And instead of a recent song,

67
00:02:19,540 --> 00:02:22,010
let's sing an old song. From a long time ago...

68
00:02:22,650 --> 00:02:24,180
(She changes the song while stuttering.)

69
00:02:25,080 --> 00:02:26,920
We'll go with an old song.

70
00:02:28,320 --> 00:02:29,750
Here we go. I'll go first.

71
00:02:30,690 --> 00:02:31,760
Tonight

72
00:02:32,020 --> 00:02:34,090
I'll send you the firefly

73
00:02:34,730 --> 00:02:36,830
- From that day - From that day

74
00:02:36,930 --> 00:02:38,960
(Stop)

75
00:02:39,360 --> 00:02:40,870
When will this be done?

76
00:02:41,370 --> 00:02:43,639
Dinner rush, and then breakfast rush

77
00:02:43,640 --> 00:02:45,499
Then prep for the next morning

78
00:02:45,500 --> 00:02:47,810
The next rush, breakfast rush, dinner rush

79
00:02:47,910 --> 00:02:49,009
(In the end, she went back to her specialty.)

80
00:02:49,010 --> 00:02:50,210
When will this be done?

81
00:02:50,340 --> 00:02:52,840
Chef Mimi, should I prep all of this celery?

82
00:02:53,240 --> 00:02:55,779
Yes, eight in total. I need eight stalks of celery.

83
00:02:55,780 --> 00:02:56,849
Got it.

84
00:02:56,850 --> 00:03:01,320
(Meanwhile, Chef Mimi is focused on chopping potatoes.)

85
00:03:02,150 --> 00:03:03,290
That's ten.

86
00:03:04,160 --> 00:03:06,290
- Yes.
- Twelve.

87
00:03:06,660 --> 00:03:07,690
(She skipped 11.)

88
00:03:08,060 --> 00:03:09,590
Who has minced garlic?

89
00:03:10,700 --> 00:03:13,260
- Tell me if you have minced garlic.
- Here it is.

90
00:03:13,800 --> 00:03:16,170
- Keep a notepad nearby...
- Thank you.

91
00:03:16,330 --> 00:03:19,339
and make a tally mark every time you finish chopping one.

92
00:03:19,340 --> 00:03:20,540
(Chuckling in embarrassment)

93
00:03:20,910 --> 00:03:22,840
(Humiliated)

94
00:03:23,040 --> 00:03:25,840
Young Ji, can you count the potatoes for me while I chop?

95
00:03:25,940 --> 00:03:28,279
I don't understand... Can you repeat it just once?

96
00:03:28,280 --> 00:03:30,549
She asked us to count the potatoes while she chops.

97
00:03:30,550 --> 00:03:32,219
How does it even work?

98
00:03:32,220 --> 00:03:34,519
I need to read your mind, don't I?

99
00:03:34,520 --> 00:03:36,419
I'm not feeling my best right now.

100
00:03:36,420 --> 00:03:37,989
Where is a wok? Oh, it's down there.

101
00:03:37,990 --> 00:03:41,060
So I skipped a number while counting.

102
00:03:41,290 --> 00:03:42,430
I was wondering what you meant.

103
00:03:44,000 --> 00:03:47,130
(Eun Ji doesn't seem to be feeling her best either.)

104
00:03:49,600 --> 00:03:50,600
(Chuckling faintly)

105
00:03:52,070 --> 00:03:54,510
(Watching Eun Ji on autopilot right in front of her)

106
00:03:54,740 --> 00:03:56,979
(She looks like an office worker ready to clock out.)

107
00:03:56,980 --> 00:03:59,039
- You're on autopilot, aren't you?
- A little bit.

108
00:03:59,040 --> 00:04:01,750
- I just need a spoon.
- I'll bring you a spoon.

109
00:04:02,750 --> 00:04:03,820
I'll use this.

110
00:04:04,580 --> 00:04:06,120
- Mimi, let me use the sink.
- Sure.

111
00:04:07,790 --> 00:04:10,960
Young Ji looks like she's aging in dog years every day.

112
00:04:11,790 --> 00:04:13,790
I think she's burned out.

113
00:04:14,690 --> 00:04:17,530
How can I be burned out every day when I haven't burned myself out?

114
00:04:18,000 --> 00:04:20,470
This is great. I just love my life.

115
00:04:21,330 --> 00:04:24,769
The head chef's constant groaning is totally killing my vibe.

116
00:04:24,770 --> 00:04:26,369
I said it was great!

117
00:04:26,370 --> 00:04:28,339
You said that with a sigh. You didn't sound convincing at all!

118
00:04:28,340 --> 00:04:29,509
There's nothing wrong with sighing,

119
00:04:29,510 --> 00:04:31,980
inhaling, or exhaling.

120
00:04:32,510 --> 00:04:34,409
Say it again, but in a happy tone this time.

121
00:04:34,410 --> 00:04:35,950
Gosh, I'm so happy.

122
00:04:37,280 --> 00:04:38,950
- I'm not doing this.
- I'm not doing this either.

123
00:04:40,750 --> 00:04:42,519
- Just wire me my money.
- Do whatever you want.

124
00:04:42,520 --> 00:04:43,720
Just send me my paycheck.

125
00:04:44,420 --> 00:04:45,619
- How much is your paycheck?
- Send me my paycheck.

126
00:04:45,620 --> 00:04:47,289
We didn't even make enough money for two shares of SK Hynix.

127
00:04:47,290 --> 00:04:48,989
What can we even do with that money, you brat?

128
00:04:48,990 --> 00:04:50,930
Did you just call me "brat?" Did you?

129
00:04:52,100 --> 00:04:53,160
"Brava."

130
00:04:54,900 --> 00:04:56,470
- Did you say "brava?"
- Brava.

131
00:04:56,570 --> 00:04:59,170
- Then it's fine. I'm sorry.
- Oh, no.

132
00:04:59,940 --> 00:05:01,570
Shall I help you measure that?

133
00:05:01,870 --> 00:05:03,540
Can you prep the other ingredients?

134
00:05:04,110 --> 00:05:06,009
- Leave it there.
- Thanks.

135
00:05:06,010 --> 00:05:08,009
Thank you for doing the dishes, Queen Eun Ji.

136
00:05:08,010 --> 00:05:10,420
- Exactly. Thank you, Eun Ji.
- Thank you so much.

137
00:05:10,820 --> 00:05:13,479
- It's all so we can go home early.
- She's like a fairy.

138
00:05:13,480 --> 00:05:14,850
You're sexy.

139
00:05:15,350 --> 00:05:17,719
- She's perfect wife material.
- Yes, she is.

140
00:05:17,720 --> 00:05:19,459
Men are lining up around the block to marry her.

141
00:05:19,460 --> 00:05:20,890
Come on. Stop it.

142
00:05:21,860 --> 00:05:25,229
Who will marry a woman like you? I, Kwak Cheol Yong, will marry you.

143
00:05:25,230 --> 00:05:26,959
Oh, come on. Seriously.

144
00:05:26,960 --> 00:05:30,129
I'm going to put you on the back of my motorcycle...

145
00:05:30,130 --> 00:05:32,670
- and take you for a ride.
- I told you not to ride that.

146
00:05:34,310 --> 00:05:37,239
That elegant lady used to be a total heartbreaker.

147
00:05:37,240 --> 00:05:39,939
I don't break anyone's heart. I make them laugh.

148
00:05:39,940 --> 00:05:42,209
She just keeps a smile on her face...

149
00:05:42,210 --> 00:05:44,149
- while dancing and singing.
- Oh, come on.

150
00:05:44,150 --> 00:05:46,220
I just dance because I'm excited.

151
00:05:47,320 --> 00:05:49,020
- They're just amazing.
- Exactly.

152
00:05:49,450 --> 00:05:52,120
- I have so much respect for them.
- Really?

153
00:05:52,620 --> 00:05:54,789
Can you check the broth for me?

154
00:05:54,790 --> 00:05:56,790
- Where is it? Here?
- Yes.

155
00:05:57,330 --> 00:06:00,200
- It needs to boil a bit longer.
- Right? I thought so.

156
00:06:00,470 --> 00:06:02,300
The aroma of the broth reminds me of Goheung.

157
00:06:02,830 --> 00:06:04,899
- Really?
- Oh, the broth.

158
00:06:04,900 --> 00:06:05,969
That's not good.

159
00:06:05,970 --> 00:06:07,340
I suddenly feel sad again.

160
00:06:08,810 --> 00:06:10,139
- I think we're done.
- Good job, everyone.

161
00:06:10,140 --> 00:06:11,979
- Good job, everyone.
- Good job, everyone.

162
00:06:11,980 --> 00:06:15,049
- See you tomorrow.
- Running a business is hard.

163
00:06:15,050 --> 00:06:16,079
I'm so tired.

164
00:06:16,080 --> 00:06:17,180
(Current Time: 11:20pm)

165
00:06:17,420 --> 00:06:20,279
- Yu Jin, will you be okay driving?
- Of course. I'll be fine.

166
00:06:20,280 --> 00:06:22,090
- Eun Ji, I'll take the other side.
- Okay.

167
00:06:22,350 --> 00:06:24,559
- Yes. Give it to me. I'll...
- Thank you, Yu Jin.

168
00:06:24,560 --> 00:06:27,390
Don't mention it. I like driving.

169
00:06:28,030 --> 00:06:30,759
- You just can't help but groan.
- I'm glad you still like driving.

170
00:06:30,760 --> 00:06:33,599
She must be tired from working all day long.

171
00:06:33,600 --> 00:06:36,169
- There's a tteokbokki place there.
- We have some competition.

172
00:06:36,170 --> 00:06:37,839
- It's us against them.
- It's right over there.

173
00:06:37,840 --> 00:06:39,800
How much are they selling their tteokbokki for?

174
00:06:40,000 --> 00:06:42,810
- You really have to stay on trend.
- I don't know why I'm so tired.

175
00:06:43,140 --> 00:06:44,809
- It's understandable.
- Right?

176
00:06:44,810 --> 00:06:46,739
We're exhausted, both mentally and physically.

177
00:06:46,740 --> 00:06:49,909
We did the Met Gala all morning and then made rice cake burgers...

178
00:06:49,910 --> 00:06:50,979
- all day long after that.
- That's right.

179
00:06:50,980 --> 00:06:54,020
- We had no time for a break.
- Mr. Kwon was waiting for us.

180
00:06:54,320 --> 00:06:55,320
- Manager Kwon.
- Exactly.

181
00:06:55,321 --> 00:06:56,390
It all happened so fast.

182
00:06:57,120 --> 00:07:01,690
(Their eventful day finally comes to an end.)

183
00:07:01,960 --> 00:07:04,130
(Eun Ji and Mimi's room)

184
00:07:04,330 --> 00:07:05,900
Dear me. My back and legs hurt.

185
00:07:07,730 --> 00:07:08,800
Gosh, my back hurts.

186
00:07:09,770 --> 00:07:10,800
(Laughing)

187
00:07:11,070 --> 00:07:12,140
(Stretching just to stay alive)

188
00:07:12,440 --> 00:07:14,939
- Mimi, it's still fun, isn't it?
- Yes.

189
00:07:14,940 --> 00:07:17,910
- It's tiring, but it's still fun.
- It's fun, indeed. It's enjoyable.

190
00:07:18,610 --> 00:07:22,880
(Young Ji and Yu Jin's room)

191
00:07:23,280 --> 00:07:27,120
(Yu Jin went to sleep first.)

192
00:07:27,320 --> 00:07:28,349
(Young Ji finished showering.)

193
00:07:28,350 --> 00:07:30,760
(She spots Yu Jin.)

194
00:07:32,190 --> 00:07:33,560
(Closing the door quietly)

195
00:07:34,890 --> 00:07:40,160
(She carefully slips into bed to avoid waking Yu Jin.)

196
00:07:41,070 --> 00:07:43,800
(So she falls asleep.)

197
00:07:44,240 --> 00:07:45,270
(Snoring)

198
00:07:47,070 --> 00:07:48,110
(Snoring)

199
00:07:50,040 --> 00:07:55,250
(Our head chef must've been really tired.)

200
00:07:56,050 --> 00:07:57,550
It will officially begin tomorrow.

201
00:07:58,620 --> 00:08:01,650
As soon as we get there, I should prep potato cream tteoksagna...

202
00:08:02,090 --> 00:08:04,690
and sticky rice cake for tteoksagna.

203
00:08:05,160 --> 00:08:06,660
I need to prep the desserts tomorrow.

204
00:08:06,960 --> 00:08:09,390
- I see.
- I didn't prep the desserts at all.

205
00:08:09,930 --> 00:08:11,730
Tomorrow will be a long day. It seemed really tiring.

206
00:08:12,000 --> 00:08:14,270
Exactly. I'll get right on that first thing tomorrow.

207
00:08:14,530 --> 00:08:17,369
You didn't see a POS machine in the kitchen, did you?

208
00:08:17,370 --> 00:08:18,700
There isn't a POS machine in the kitchen.

209
00:08:19,140 --> 00:08:22,169
Exactly. So do we have to call out the orders to you every single time?

210
00:08:22,170 --> 00:08:24,580
I'm curious about how that works.

211
00:08:24,680 --> 00:08:26,180
We should talk about it tomorrow.

212
00:08:26,940 --> 00:08:29,450
The serving system is so high-end. I don't think I can handle it.

213
00:08:29,680 --> 00:08:31,920
- So is the kitchen.
- I know, right? It's so fancy.

214
00:08:32,220 --> 00:08:35,250
(The night of anxiety has passed.)

215
00:08:35,450 --> 00:08:39,020
(Downtown is full of life on this bustling Sunday.)

216
00:08:39,420 --> 00:08:42,890
(The bright sunlight welcomes a brand new day.)

217
00:08:43,360 --> 00:08:46,760
(Today is the grand opening of the 2nd branch.)

218
00:08:47,060 --> 00:08:51,100
(What will happen at the 2nd branch?)

219
00:08:51,340 --> 00:08:52,400
(Space Rice Cake seems popular these days.)

220
00:08:56,340 --> 00:08:58,510
(Current Time: 8:50am)

221
00:08:58,710 --> 00:09:01,179
- Yu Jin, Young Ji isn't up, is she?
- No.

222
00:09:01,180 --> 00:09:02,250
I'll wake her up.

223
00:09:03,310 --> 00:09:04,480
(Knocking)

224
00:09:04,680 --> 00:09:06,050
Your Majesty.

225
00:09:07,620 --> 00:09:09,989
- Yes?
- Please forgive me for waking you.

226
00:09:09,990 --> 00:09:11,259
Your Majesty.

227
00:09:11,260 --> 00:09:14,290
You need to wake up now so that we can go to work.

228
00:09:14,990 --> 00:09:16,860
(Walking with short steps)

229
00:09:17,130 --> 00:09:19,129
- Your Majesty.
- Your Majesty.

230
00:09:19,130 --> 00:09:21,799
Did you enjoy a peaceful slumber last night?

231
00:09:21,800 --> 00:09:24,539
- May I offer you some arginine?
- Did you enjoy...

232
00:09:24,540 --> 00:09:25,740
No, that's okay.

233
00:09:26,240 --> 00:09:27,669
- Your Majesty.
- Your face... Who are you?

234
00:09:27,670 --> 00:09:29,670
Your Majesty, you snored so loudly...

235
00:09:30,010 --> 00:09:32,310
earlier this morning.

236
00:09:32,540 --> 00:09:34,179
- I'm sorry.
- You must've been tired.

237
00:09:34,180 --> 00:09:35,949
- No problem, Your Majesty.
- It's all right.

238
00:09:35,950 --> 00:09:38,549
- Hearing you snore...
- Yes.

239
00:09:38,550 --> 00:09:41,689
- makes me happy.
- Yes.

240
00:09:41,690 --> 00:09:44,360
- Please wake up and come out.
- Okay.

241
00:09:45,220 --> 00:09:47,630
(Very well. You may all withdraw now.)

242
00:09:47,860 --> 00:09:49,859
Three thousand people are tracking the waitlist on CatchTable.

243
00:09:49,860 --> 00:09:51,230
- Pardon?
- Three thousand.

244
00:09:51,660 --> 00:09:52,660
Oh, three thousand?

245
00:09:53,730 --> 00:09:55,800
(The reservation system opened on the grand opening day.)

246
00:09:56,000 --> 00:09:57,339
(About 3,000 people are waiting to book a table.)

247
00:09:57,340 --> 00:09:58,670
(3,182 users are tracking the waitlist!)

248
00:09:59,070 --> 00:10:00,070
They're tracking the waitlist right now?

249
00:10:00,810 --> 00:10:03,810
- When does it go live?
- At 10am.

250
00:10:04,480 --> 00:10:07,579
So are they going to book a table as soon as it goes live?

251
00:10:07,580 --> 00:10:09,810
(The popularity of the shop doesn't feel real.)

252
00:10:10,050 --> 00:10:11,749
Young Ji, 3,000 people are...

253
00:10:11,750 --> 00:10:13,780
tracking the waitlist on CatchTable right now...

254
00:10:13,950 --> 00:10:15,350
to swoop in at 10am when it goes live.

255
00:10:15,850 --> 00:10:17,589
(The head chef shudders under pressure.)

256
00:10:17,590 --> 00:10:18,620
I want to go home.

257
00:10:19,060 --> 00:10:22,090
- Can you handle 3,000 tables?
- Let's go home. It's now or never.

258
00:10:22,960 --> 00:10:25,230
Oh, boy. What do I do?

259
00:10:26,330 --> 00:10:29,300
- How about I try to book a table?
- Go ahead.

260
00:10:29,470 --> 00:10:31,499
The number of current users is 3,825.

261
00:10:31,500 --> 00:10:32,869
Why would there be 3,825 people...

262
00:10:32,870 --> 00:10:34,739
- waiting to book a table...
- It'll keep going up until 10am.

263
00:10:34,740 --> 00:10:35,769
I'm terrified.

264
00:10:35,770 --> 00:10:37,739
How come a staggering 3,825 people are...

265
00:10:37,740 --> 00:10:39,380
waiting to book a table at our restaurant?

266
00:10:39,910 --> 00:10:43,150
How come so many distinguished people are...

267
00:10:43,710 --> 00:10:45,580
interested in our restaurant?

268
00:10:45,880 --> 00:10:47,080
I'm getting so nervous.

269
00:10:47,390 --> 00:10:49,349
- Eun Ji, I'm nervous.
- Me too.

270
00:10:49,350 --> 00:10:50,419
(Don't worry. Even if you fail, you guys should still go.)

271
00:10:50,420 --> 00:10:51,460
It's 10am now. Is it open yet?

272
00:10:52,020 --> 00:10:53,320
(Current Time: 10am)

273
00:10:53,560 --> 00:10:55,059
(Reservations are now open.)

274
00:10:55,060 --> 00:10:57,760
- My gosh. It's already over.
- What?

275
00:10:58,100 --> 00:11:01,170
(All tables are fully booked in a flash.)

276
00:11:01,500 --> 00:11:03,469
Exactly. What's going on? I clicked the button.

277
00:11:03,470 --> 00:11:04,799
But it said it was already fully booked.

278
00:11:04,800 --> 00:11:07,100
"You have failed to reserve a table."

279
00:11:07,270 --> 00:11:08,440
Eun Ji, it's over.

280
00:11:08,540 --> 00:11:10,709
- I'm speechless.
- My goodness.

281
00:11:10,710 --> 00:11:12,039
- Let's get going.
- Let's go.

282
00:11:12,040 --> 00:11:13,080
Let's go.

283
00:11:13,280 --> 00:11:14,880
Are you all mentally prepared for today?

284
00:11:16,110 --> 00:11:19,020
- There's a cap on table bookings.
- That's right.

285
00:11:19,550 --> 00:11:21,350
- Above all...
- I'm thrilled by the attention.

286
00:11:21,450 --> 00:11:23,350
- Above all, I'm grateful.
- Right.

287
00:11:23,690 --> 00:11:25,289
- Today is Sunday, right?
- Yes.

288
00:11:25,290 --> 00:11:27,890
- Yeonhui-dong is packed on Sundays.
- My point exactly.

289
00:11:28,890 --> 00:11:29,960
Why is today Sunday?

290
00:11:30,360 --> 00:11:31,899
- Why is it Sunday?
- Why is it Sunday?

291
00:11:31,900 --> 00:11:33,430
How come it's already Sunday?

292
00:11:33,830 --> 00:11:34,830
- That's exactly my point.
- When did we start?

293
00:11:34,831 --> 00:11:37,870
- I've totally lost track of time.
- Me too.

294
00:11:38,170 --> 00:11:39,699
I think we started last Saturday or Sunday.

295
00:11:39,700 --> 00:11:41,270
Has it been over a week since we started working on this?

296
00:11:41,770 --> 00:11:42,770
It's been about a week.

297
00:11:42,910 --> 00:11:44,479
(It's been exactly a week since they started the business.)

298
00:11:44,480 --> 00:11:46,640
- Almost a week.
- Wait. What is that waiting line?

299
00:11:47,480 --> 00:11:50,280
- No way. That can't be.
- No way.

300
00:11:51,620 --> 00:11:54,289
(An endless line stretches out in front of the Earth Arcaders.)

301
00:11:54,290 --> 00:11:56,989
- No, that can't be.
- No way.

302
00:11:56,990 --> 00:11:58,559
(They're so flustered that they can only say, "No way.")

303
00:11:58,560 --> 00:12:00,019
- No way.
- Seriously?

304
00:12:00,020 --> 00:12:01,059
- It's not what you think.
- No.

305
00:12:01,060 --> 00:12:02,290
- No, right?
- Right?

306
00:12:02,590 --> 00:12:04,029
Why is everyone lining up?

307
00:12:04,030 --> 00:12:05,699
- It seems like there are...
- Something must be happening.

308
00:12:05,700 --> 00:12:06,999
many stores and events here.

309
00:12:07,000 --> 00:12:10,069
- Honesty, humility, ahk.
- Humility, ahk.

310
00:12:10,070 --> 00:12:12,339
- Nice.
- Thank you.

311
00:12:12,340 --> 00:12:13,770
Thank you.

312
00:12:13,940 --> 00:12:15,309
We're going to work.

313
00:12:15,310 --> 00:12:16,640
I don't want to work.

314
00:12:17,440 --> 00:12:19,180
What did I do to deserve having to go to work?

315
00:12:19,240 --> 00:12:21,279
(Going to work while groaning)

316
00:12:21,280 --> 00:12:22,780
We got rice cakes from the HQ.

317
00:12:24,010 --> 00:12:27,020
(Now that they've become a major franchise...)

318
00:12:27,250 --> 00:12:28,850
Girls, let's bring in the rice cakes.

319
00:12:29,220 --> 00:12:30,290
Okay, Eun Ji.

320
00:12:30,860 --> 00:12:32,019
One, two, three.

321
00:12:32,020 --> 00:12:33,020
(They'll be delivered to their doorstep every day.)

322
00:12:33,021 --> 00:12:34,929
- Shall we take them to the pantry?
- Yes.

323
00:12:34,930 --> 00:12:36,190
Let's go to the pantry first.

324
00:12:36,430 --> 00:12:38,129
(These rice cakes are freshly made today.)

325
00:12:38,130 --> 00:12:39,860
It's heavy, Your Majesty.

326
00:12:40,430 --> 00:12:42,799
(We'll introduce sponsored items from the HQ other than rice cakes.)

327
00:12:42,800 --> 00:12:44,570
Good morning. This is...

328
00:12:45,200 --> 00:12:47,240
the last glimpse of me looking decent today.

329
00:12:47,270 --> 00:12:50,239
(Showing off her decency)

330
00:12:50,240 --> 00:12:53,079
(Perk 1, the uniform)

331
00:12:53,080 --> 00:12:54,180
Hello, customer.

332
00:12:54,780 --> 00:12:56,510
- Would you like to order?
- My gosh.

333
00:12:57,080 --> 00:12:59,280
You look like the magical...

334
00:12:59,450 --> 00:13:00,649
I like this shirt.

335
00:13:00,650 --> 00:13:03,120
I look like someone who works at a burger place overseas.

336
00:13:03,790 --> 00:13:06,420
So today, I'll wear a waist apron...

337
00:13:06,920 --> 00:13:08,760
so the shirt is more visible.

338
00:13:09,790 --> 00:13:12,760
(Perk 2, POS system)

339
00:13:12,800 --> 00:13:15,499
We'll go and take a look at the POS system.

340
00:13:15,500 --> 00:13:16,899
- Okay.
- Go ahead.

341
00:13:16,900 --> 00:13:18,970
- Hello.
- Hello.

342
00:13:19,500 --> 00:13:21,239
I made a reservation through CatchTable.

343
00:13:21,240 --> 00:13:23,239
- Is it a reservation for two?
- That's right.

344
00:13:23,240 --> 00:13:24,309
Okay.

345
00:13:24,310 --> 00:13:26,109
Take a look at our menu...

346
00:13:26,110 --> 00:13:27,440
and tell me what you think.

347
00:13:27,510 --> 00:13:29,249
- I'd like...
- Yes?

348
00:13:29,250 --> 00:13:30,779
Too much rice cake in a burger

349
00:13:30,780 --> 00:13:32,449
One shrimp burger set.

350
00:13:32,450 --> 00:13:33,849
One moment, please.

351
00:13:33,850 --> 00:13:35,289
(A customer who knows the menu names suspiciously well)

352
00:13:35,290 --> 00:13:37,489
- Is it just 1, not 2?
- Yes, just 1.

353
00:13:37,490 --> 00:13:39,519
All right, ma'am.

354
00:13:39,520 --> 00:13:41,360
This is a little painful.

355
00:13:41,460 --> 00:13:42,460
(The POS system isn’t as easy as it seemed.)

356
00:13:42,461 --> 00:13:44,630
- Please hurry.
- Okay.

357
00:13:44,700 --> 00:13:45,959
I'm starving.

358
00:13:45,960 --> 00:13:47,399
I waited for a long time.

359
00:13:47,400 --> 00:13:48,929
Why did I have to wait when I made a reservation?

360
00:13:48,930 --> 00:13:50,869
One zesty pomegranate ade,

361
00:13:50,870 --> 00:13:52,439
one do you like mint? of carrot! cake,

362
00:13:52,440 --> 00:13:55,139
and one too much rice cake in a burger, shrimp. Is that right?

363
00:13:55,140 --> 00:13:57,980
- Yes. I'll pay by card.
- All right.

364
00:13:58,487 --> 00:13:59,927
Please give me my table number.

365
00:14:01,780 --> 00:14:03,850
Thank you. Hurry up. I'm hungry.

366
00:14:04,250 --> 00:14:05,279
(It seems like there's a long way to go.)

367
00:14:05,280 --> 00:14:06,519
You can do this.

368
00:14:06,520 --> 00:14:07,789
It's much more convenient.

369
00:14:07,790 --> 00:14:10,960
(Starting prep for the new menu at the revamped 2nd branch)

370
00:14:11,890 --> 00:14:13,089
Let's go.

371
00:14:13,090 --> 00:14:14,760
(Keeping themselves clean at the 2nd branch as well)

372
00:14:14,860 --> 00:14:16,859
Keep smiling, everyone.

373
00:14:16,860 --> 00:14:18,160
Okay.

374
00:14:18,452 --> 00:14:19,852
Evil spirits, go away!

375
00:14:20,100 --> 00:14:22,330
- Stay away, evil spirits.
- Let's keep it beautiful.

376
00:14:22,530 --> 00:14:25,899
(Irony of sending off evil spirits with "fire" on her forehead)

377
00:14:25,900 --> 00:14:28,770
(The head chef starts by making the rice cake bun.)

378
00:14:28,810 --> 00:14:31,179
(Placing the mold on top of gijeongtteok)

379
00:14:31,180 --> 00:14:33,679
(Putting her weight onto it and pressing down firmly)

380
00:14:33,680 --> 00:14:36,179
Give it one final good twist while pressing down.

381
00:14:36,180 --> 00:14:37,350
That's perfect.

382
00:14:38,073 --> 00:14:39,113
It's perfect.

383
00:14:39,495 --> 00:14:40,995
I'll take it now.

384
00:14:41,020 --> 00:14:43,019
Since it leaves some scraps behind,

385
00:14:43,020 --> 00:14:45,260
- Okay.
- it's fun to cut them.

386
00:14:45,697 --> 00:14:46,866
The zero-waste style.

387
00:14:46,960 --> 00:14:48,790
(They're used in the carrot cake instead of being thrown away.)

388
00:14:49,360 --> 00:14:50,490
(Shaking)

389
00:14:51,100 --> 00:14:53,529
Like in TWS's song, you have to be a little whiny.

390
00:14:53,530 --> 00:14:54,869
(Whining)

391
00:14:54,870 --> 00:14:55,929
Like this.

392
00:14:55,930 --> 00:14:58,400
Then it comes off.

393
00:14:58,540 --> 00:15:00,669
(Whining)

394
00:15:00,670 --> 00:15:02,439
(Whining)

395
00:15:02,440 --> 00:15:06,479
(It's awkward, but it's surprisingly effective.)

396
00:15:06,480 --> 00:15:08,450
Can someone call TWS for me?

397
00:15:08,910 --> 00:15:09,910
That'd make me happy.

398
00:15:10,610 --> 00:15:11,920
Am I not enough?

399
00:15:12,520 --> 00:15:13,949
- What?
- Am I not enough for you?

400
00:15:13,950 --> 00:15:15,750
Gosh, that came out wrong.

401
00:15:16,090 --> 00:15:17,449
I'm really cute, you know.

402
00:15:17,450 --> 00:15:18,719
Of course.

403
00:15:18,720 --> 00:15:20,989
(Yu Jin is cute.)

404
00:15:20,990 --> 00:15:22,159
Come on, Cheol Yong.

405
00:15:22,160 --> 00:15:24,659
I thought you only liked me, but you flirt with everyone.

406
00:15:24,660 --> 00:15:26,299
I didn't know you were here, Jeong Hye.

407
00:15:26,300 --> 00:15:28,100
- Goodness.
- Oh, no.

408
00:15:28,700 --> 00:15:30,130
I'm hurt.

409
00:15:30,200 --> 00:15:33,140
(Kwak Cheol Yong is a heartbreaker.)

410
00:15:33,170 --> 00:15:34,310
Shall we kiss?

411
00:15:34,810 --> 00:15:37,139
(Offering an appeasement that has no chance of working)

412
00:15:37,140 --> 00:15:38,880
I don't want to kiss you.

413
00:15:38,940 --> 00:15:40,739
(Sulking)

414
00:15:40,740 --> 00:15:42,680
You keep slipping right out of my hands.

415
00:15:43,380 --> 00:15:45,779
My Jeong Hye, shall we kiss?

416
00:15:45,780 --> 00:15:47,619
How about we go to Portugal someday,

417
00:15:47,620 --> 00:15:48,889
fix up an old house, and live there?

418
00:15:48,890 --> 00:15:51,059
But first, you have to kiss me.

419
00:15:51,060 --> 00:15:52,659
Then everything will fall right into place.

420
00:15:52,660 --> 00:15:54,329
My goodness.

421
00:15:54,330 --> 00:15:55,330
Nothing will move forward...

422
00:15:55,331 --> 00:15:57,389
if you won't even hold my hand or kiss me.

423
00:15:57,390 --> 00:15:59,299
You're so naughty.

424
00:15:59,300 --> 00:16:02,029
- Shall we kiss first?
- Goodness.

425
00:16:02,030 --> 00:16:03,030
Are you two kissing again?

426
00:16:03,031 --> 00:16:05,669
If you work well today, I'll think about it.

427
00:16:05,670 --> 00:16:07,840
Thank you, Jeong Hye. You're a fox.

428
00:16:08,670 --> 00:16:09,939
I'm a fox with no tail.

429
00:16:09,940 --> 00:16:12,040
- Overdrive.
- You're a wolf with no tail.

430
00:16:12,610 --> 00:16:14,180
You make me overdrive.

431
00:16:14,310 --> 00:16:17,610
(After all that lovers' quarrel)

432
00:16:17,750 --> 00:16:19,850
I finished making all the gijeongtteok for today.

433
00:16:20,450 --> 00:16:23,589
- You're the best.
- Including the batch for dinner.

434
00:16:23,590 --> 00:16:24,890
(Fully prepped with rice cake buns to keep going through dinner)

435
00:16:24,960 --> 00:16:27,990
(Next is making the patties.)

436
00:16:28,530 --> 00:16:30,130
About this much is 170g.

437
00:16:30,890 --> 00:16:31,959
(She starts dribbling the beef patty with both hands.)

438
00:16:31,960 --> 00:16:33,100
It looks like a basketball.

439
00:16:34,300 --> 00:16:37,800
(Giving it a nice, neat shape at the end)

440
00:16:38,140 --> 00:16:42,140
(All she has to do is repeat this process dozens of times.)

441
00:16:45,640 --> 00:16:47,540
There's no soul in the chef's eyes.

442
00:16:48,250 --> 00:16:50,880
(When the head chef feels empty inside, )

443
00:16:51,010 --> 00:16:53,850
(it's time for the sous chef's shrimp patty beat.)

444
00:16:53,920 --> 00:16:55,389
We are martial arts masters.

445
00:16:55,390 --> 00:16:56,650
This is all part of our training.

446
00:16:56,690 --> 00:16:58,560
(Training in progress)

447
00:16:58,590 --> 00:17:01,890
(The shrimp patties made by a martial arts master)

448
00:17:02,060 --> 00:17:05,059
(Chopping the shrimp...)

449
00:17:05,060 --> 00:17:08,030
(and grinding them)

450
00:17:08,130 --> 00:17:11,269
(Shape them nicely into round patties)

451
00:17:11,270 --> 00:17:13,270
(Flour)

452
00:17:13,570 --> 00:17:16,109
Shrimp patties should cost over 13 dollars.

453
00:17:16,110 --> 00:17:18,609
- More is coming. Excuse me.
- Go ahead.

454
00:17:18,610 --> 00:17:21,179
(When coated evenly, the shrimp patty prep is complete.)

455
00:17:21,180 --> 00:17:24,080
(The dessert team is preparing the carrot cake.)

456
00:17:24,110 --> 00:17:25,719
Making sponge cake crumbs...

457
00:17:25,720 --> 00:17:27,150
from scratch is a lot of work.

458
00:17:27,650 --> 00:17:29,119
I keep looking for the store-bought ones.

459
00:17:29,120 --> 00:17:30,319
(Making sponge cake crumbs by hand)

460
00:17:30,320 --> 00:17:33,490
(Yu Jin is shaping the carrot rice cakes.)

461
00:17:33,660 --> 00:17:37,330
(When the beautiful orange dough is shaped this way and that, )

462
00:17:37,530 --> 00:17:40,500
(the carrot rice cakes that look just like real carrots are ready.)

463
00:17:40,800 --> 00:17:43,430
(Our cute, little carrots)

464
00:17:43,570 --> 00:17:45,740
(I'm going to fry you all up)

465
00:17:45,870 --> 00:17:48,410
(Somebody, save me!)

466
00:17:48,510 --> 00:17:50,870
(With everything prepared)

467
00:17:51,070 --> 00:17:52,309
They look like real carrots.

468
00:17:52,310 --> 00:17:54,140
(Deep-fry the carrot rice cakes until they become plump.)

469
00:17:54,210 --> 00:17:57,650
(The carrot cake is ready.)

470
00:17:57,710 --> 00:18:00,020
I'll make some pomegranate ade now.

471
00:18:00,650 --> 00:18:01,650
Did you cut the onions?

472
00:18:01,650 --> 00:18:02,650
(Eun Ji practices making the pomegranate ade.)

473
00:18:02,651 --> 00:18:03,790
They're over there.

474
00:18:04,050 --> 00:18:05,119
(Adding plenty of sweet pomegranate syrup)

475
00:18:05,120 --> 00:18:06,890
- I...
- How do you do it?

476
00:18:07,190 --> 00:18:10,590
(A full cup of ice)

477
00:18:10,790 --> 00:18:13,230
(Giving it a nice, refreshing chill)

478
00:18:13,600 --> 00:18:17,200
(Pouring in plenty of sparkling water)

479
00:18:17,330 --> 00:18:20,669
(Top it with a sprig of rosemary, and it's done.)

480
00:18:20,670 --> 00:18:25,310
(Mimi, our resident sweet-tooth, gives it a taste.)

481
00:18:26,380 --> 00:18:27,380
The syrup is delicious.

482
00:18:27,410 --> 00:18:28,779
(The younger members take a sip.)

483
00:18:28,780 --> 00:18:29,880
It looks so good.

484
00:18:30,410 --> 00:18:31,650
The syrup is good.

485
00:18:32,480 --> 00:18:33,849
- Eun Ji, this is amazing.
- Do I just chew it?

486
00:18:33,850 --> 00:18:34,989
You can chew and eat it.

487
00:18:34,990 --> 00:18:36,519
(Nodding)

488
00:18:36,520 --> 00:18:37,919
Gosh, this is insane.

489
00:18:37,920 --> 00:18:40,260
This syrup is good. I should buy some for myself.

490
00:18:40,560 --> 00:18:42,160
- The syrup is insanely good.
- Eun Ji, it's good.

491
00:18:42,590 --> 00:18:44,629
I can taste the scent of Goheung right now.

492
00:18:44,630 --> 00:18:46,199
You can smell Goheung because of the pomegranate?

493
00:18:46,200 --> 00:18:47,259
Yes.

494
00:18:47,260 --> 00:18:49,330
(The pomegranate ade is approved.)

495
00:18:49,700 --> 00:18:51,469
Everyone, it's 1:00pm.

496
00:18:51,470 --> 00:18:53,970
- We're opening.
- We're opening.

497
00:18:54,140 --> 00:18:56,139
(The 1st day of business at their 2nd branch)

498
00:18:56,140 --> 00:18:57,540
We are open.

499
00:18:58,880 --> 00:19:00,780
- We are.
- We can do this.

500
00:19:01,380 --> 00:19:02,380
Honesty.

501
00:19:02,381 --> 00:19:04,309
- Humility. Ahk.
- Humility. Ahk.

502
00:19:04,310 --> 00:19:05,319
Here we go.

503
00:19:05,320 --> 00:19:07,120
I'm nervous.

504
00:19:07,420 --> 00:19:10,250
(With her heart fluttering, she goes towards the door.)

505
00:19:11,220 --> 00:19:12,289
(Peeking)

506
00:19:12,290 --> 00:19:13,890
(Peeking)

